  "citations": [
    {
      "start": 3581,
      "end": 3588,
      "previousStart": 3579,
      "previousEnd": 3586,
      "text": "On mutation POSTs to operation command targets, authorities MUST ignore the\n`BDP-Minimum-Scope-Position`, `BDP-Scope-Epoch`, and\n`BDP-Authorization-View` request fields. Their presence, absence, completeness,\nand field values do not impose a minimum-position barrier or affect command\nidentity. Ordinary HTTP field syntax and transport, header, and body bounds\nstill apply, as do authorization, idempotency, carrier validation, and\n`expectedRevision`. This rule applies to mutation POSTs under this profile and\ncumulative profiles. It does not change conditions on reads.",
      "sha256": "9260b06fa9c1b71c7fa63696183bbb270d00ab1ad02a4a682658f4a10fc63596",
      "unchangedText": true
    },
    {
      "start": 5818,
      "end": 5822,
      "previousStart": 5797,
      "previousEnd": 5801,
      "text": "Transactional mutation POSTs follow the shared\n[mutation command preconditions](#mutation-command-preconditions): copied read\nminimum fields impose no barrier or command-identity input. This does not change\nminimum controls on reads, including subsequent Mutation Receipt GET or HEAD\nrequests.",
      "sha256": "4bcdae0dec55dd440429a5c0b2790ab4d930fc9b347a5863bf70abec175231cd",
      "unchangedText": true
    },
    {
      "start": 5853,
      "end": 5855,
      "previousStart": 5832,
      "previousEnd": 5834,
      "text": "The inherited [Mutation command preconditions](#mutation-command-preconditions)\nalso apply here: HTTP conditional fields on operation command targets do not\nguard newly produced receipts.",
      "sha256": "d503844b42944f07a8d048cb8fe0888f696d12d4e9373b8d62ef4bab6a542f00",
      "unchangedText": true
    }
